.TH BEYRIX 1 "2026-11-24" "Beyrix 0.1.0-alpha.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
beyrix \- experimental Wayland terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beyrix
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beyrix
is an experimental terminal emulator for Linux and Wayland.
It renders with OpenGL ES through EGL and falls back to software rendering
when hardware acceleration is unavailable.
The interactive session runs Bash through a pseudo-terminal.
.PP
Run without arguments to open a new window.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B open
Open a new terminal window.
.TP
.B theme
Print the active theme.
.TP
.B theme list
List the built-in themes: minimal, developer and signature.
.TP
.BI "theme set " NAME
Save a theme and update the current window when a control socket is available.
.TP
.B layout [list]
Show the cursor layout. The supported layouts are as-is, bottom and bottom-input.
.TP
.BI "layout set " NAME
Save the cursor layout.
.TP
.B renderer [list]
Show the rendering backend. The supported values are auto, opengl, vulkan and
software. The Vulkan backend is diagnostics only; selecting it falls back to
software rendering.
.TP
.BI "renderer set " NAME
Save the rendering backend.
.TP
.B gpu
Print the detected GPUs, graphics APIs and the selected backend.
.TP
.BI "edit " FILE
Open FILE in the built-in editor.
.TP
.B --pty
Run Bash in the current terminal instead of opening a window.
.TP
.B --help
Print the command summary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BEYRIX_CONTROL_SOCKET
Control socket used to notify a running window about configuration changes.
.TP
.B BEYRIX_PROMPT_THEME
Path to the prompt theme file used by the Bash integration.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the configuration file
.IR beyrix/config.toml .
The legacy
.I beynal/config.toml
is migrated when the new file does not exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/beyrix/config.toml
User configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation is installed in
.I /usr/share/doc/beyrix/
and at
.IR https://github.com/Beykus-Y/Beyrix .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/Beykus-Y/Beyrix/issues.